    "pressure": {
      "file": "fire_and_gas_detection_system_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Coverage: see the fire, smell the gas — then act",
      "description": "F&G detectors are placed by coverage mapping: flame detectors have a cone of vision (≈ 90° for UV/IR) and a range for a given fire size; gas detectors are placed where leaks would collect (low for heavier-than-air gas, high for lighter) and open-path detectors guard boundaries. Typical alarm levels: 20 % LEL low, 50–60 % LEL high. The F&G logic uses voting (e.g. 2-out-of-N confirmed) to start executive actions: shutdown and isolation, deluge, ventilation changes and alarms.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
